  1. Hand-built battery (probe.mjs, ~75 fixtures, each run through gate `check`, gate `escalate-scan` and TREE parse() in a child
     process with a 25 s timeout): critical.globs/test.globs/manifest as directory, dangling link, symlink loop, FIFO, /dev/null,
     /dev/zero link, Unix socket, mode 000, /proc/self/mem link, CESU surrogate bytes, overlong, >U+10FFFF, UTF-16LE, NUL bytes,
     BOM-only, CRLF, empty, comment-only, whitespace-only, 5 MB one-line glob; manifests/ as mode 000 / --x / r-- / regular file /
     dangling link; older and current manifests; sidecar as FIFO / dir / dangling / mode 000 / non-UTF-8 / socket / /proc link;
     tiers 1, 2, 3; LC_ALL=C + PYTHONUTF8=0 + PYTHONCOERCECLOCALE=0 with non-ASCII paths. Result: every unreadable kind ->
     gate refuses with `critical-glob-unreadable` on the stdout FAIL line, exactly ONE `unreadable` stderr line naming the path
     (or the evaluator failure), scan writes `REASON: critical-glob-unreadable` (TARGET_TIER 2 at tier 1, 3 at tier 2, no flag at
     tier 3), parse() flagged with the same token; no hang (FIFO/zero/socket never opened, each case <130 ms); parse() never threw
     on a current manifest/sidecar oddity. Clean kinds (empty, BOM, CRLF, comment-only, symlink-to-readable incl. relative and
     absolute, non-ASCII manifest under LC_ALL=C, `t..files`, `t.files`/`t.1.files.bak` (not matching the glob), an unreadable
     manifest of ANOTHER task) accept with EMPTY stderr and derived 'accepted'.
  2. Randomised differential (fuzz.mjs, seeds 11/23 default locale, 77 under LC_ALL=C PYTHONUTF8=0): 1000 fixtures combining
     critical.globs kind x test.globs kind x 0-2 older manifests of 11 kinds x tier x attempt. Asserted per run: gate check exit 0
     <=> derived 'accepted'; same reason token (unreadable vs plain critical-glob) in gate stdout and parse mismatch; one
