     surface as rc 1 -> unreadable anyway.
  4. UTF-8 validity parity: 30 000 random byte strings (biased to lead/continuation/surrogate/overlong bytes): Python strict
     `decode('utf-8')` vs `TextDecoder('utf-8',{fatal:true})` -> 0 mismatches.
  5. `done`: two accepted rows + directory critical.globs -> both rows refused naming the token, one diagnostic per row evaluation,
