  6. Cost: 30 MB critical.globs: gate 4.26 s (post-CD2) vs 4.33 s (new), memory 245 MB vs 480 MB - no time regression.
  Worker's extension (an existing but unlistable manifests/ -> unreadable): compatible hardening, NOT a contradiction. Pinned
  semantics 1 says "no entry matches -> no hit" and the Rule says "failing to read for any other reason -> UNREADABLE"; with an
  unlistable directory "no entry matches" cannot be established, so the base's silent no-hit is exactly the fail-open this task
  removes, and the deviation only ever flags (never accepts). Gate and parse agree on it (mode 000, --x, r--, a regular file, a
  dangling link; all reject with the token) and both shipped suites pin it (run_escalate u12, parse UNREADABLE_INPUTS). It is
  not covered by accept.sh; the lead may want to note it in ruling CD-i. Observation, not FAIL.

