OBSERVATIONS (backlog; none is a FAIL under rule 5 or the acceptance criteria)
 O1. Gate-vs-parse disagreement on a NON-UTF-8 manifest ENTRY NAME (probe N20): `manifests/t.0<0xff>.files` holding a clean
     path. Gate: python opens it byte-exact via surrogateescape -> no hit -> `check` exits 0. parse(): fs.readdirSync decodes the
     name lossily (U+FFFD), stat ENOENT -> unreadable -> derived 'flagged' (conservative direction). The base agreed on this
     fixture (both accepted), so the disagreement is new, but it needs a hand-made invalid-UTF-8 file name in .swarm/manifests
     (task ids/attempts are ASCII), it is the same lossy-name limitation every readdirSync in parse.mjs already has, and it is not
     among the brief's enumerated kinds (permission-denied, invalid UTF-8 content, directory). Variant N44 (same name holding a
     real hit): gate `critical-glob`, parse `critical-glob-unreadable`; both refuse (base parse ACCEPTED it, so this improved).
     Fix if wanted: readdirSync(dir, {encoding:'buffer'}) and Buffer paths. Same fixture where the content is unreadable: gate
     prints `evaluator failed (UnicodeEncodeError)` instead of naming the path (still exactly one line, still fail-closed).
 O2. No shipped test for a dangling or looping test.globs (see (e) g03/p03).
 O3. No test drives the evaluator's outer `except` (g14/p07) or the unlistable-manifests case through accept.sh.
